<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">North America</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">North America is the continent comprising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. From the seventeenth century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> competed there for colonies and trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> confirmed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> as the dominant colonial power in North America, before the American colonies won independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/north-america.jpg" alt="North America" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bosonic dressing · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_North_America.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
